#=GF RT Structure of the dengue virus RNA promoter.
#=GF RA Sun YT, Varani G
#=GF RL RNA. 2022;28:1210-1223.
#=GF CC Flavivirus stem-loop A (SLA) is a secondary structure present in the 5
#=GF CC prime untranslated (5'-UTR) region of viruses of the genus Flavivirus. SLA
#=GF CC structure was first proposed from enzymatic and chemical probing methods
#=GF CC [1,2] afterwards the 3D structure of Dengue (PDB:7LYF, 7LYG) and Zika
#=GF CC (PDB:5U0B) SLA viruses were reported [3]. SLA interacts with the
#=GF CC nonstructural protein 5 (NS5), where SLA functions as a promoter for viral
#=GF CC RNA synthesis by NS5 polymerase. The SLA secondary structure includes a
#=GF CC bottom stem-loop (previously reported as SL1 and SL2), a top stem-loop
#=GF CC (previously reported as SL3 and TL) and a side-loop (previously proposed
#=GF CC as side SL). The side SL variate in length between flaviviruses
#=GF CC (Tick-borne flaviviruses present a side SL >40nt), despite the lack of
#=GF CC sequence conservation, deletion of the side SL abolish replication in
#=GF CC Dengue virus. It is proposed that the side SL is essential to maintain the
#=GF CC overall fold of Flavivirus SLA [3]. SLA 3D was also reported in PDB:7UMC,
#=GF CC 8GZP, 8GZQ [4, 5].
#=GF WK Flavivirus
#=GF SQ 15

